  "notes": [
    "Control path: HTTP GET http://<host>/remote.cgi?<command>[=<value>] to a MADRIX Aura 2/8/12/32 (src/main.js sendCommand); the connection setting is only the host. There is no reply parsing and no state is read back, so the module has no feedbacks. Only 'last_command' and 'last_status' variables exist (src/variables.js).",
    "The Aura only accepts these commands after matching <remote ... porttype=\"http\" ...> lines were added to its ShowConfig.xml (companion/HELP.md); without them the commands have no effect. Not tested against a device.",
    "Commands sent per action: playback_state sends play, pause or stop; intensity sends intensity=<value>, intensityinc=<step> or intensitydec=<step>; speed sends speed=<value>, speedinc=<step> or speeddec=<step>; cue sends cue=<number>; previous_cue sends previous; next_cue sends next; record sends record or stop; group_intensity sends group<N>=<value>, group<N>inc=<step> or group<N>dec=<step>.",
    "playback_state in toggle mode keeps its own state in the module (initially empty): the first press sends Toggle State 2, then alternates. The state is not read from the device and is not changed by other actions. record keeps a local flag and alternates record and stop; any sent 'stop' command resets that flag (src/main.js:88).",
    "Value ranges 0-255 (cue 1-255) are the number-field limits of the source; the device behavior outside them is not documented in the module.",
    "Scope: this module covers the MADRIX Aura hardware nodes only. Other MADRIX products (MADRIX 5 software, MADRIX 3, MADRIX Luna and other hardware) have no Companion module; see noModule in _index.json.",
    "Source repository bitfocus/companion-module-madrix-aura; the same source also exists as verledung/companion-module-madrix-aura (author's repository, src identical at the inspected commits, last commit 2026-01-29).",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.14.1: options do not support expressions. Complete list of the 8 actions found in the source."
  ]
